// RFC 0031 root-set oracle #2 (exit 42) — the #[export] root.
//
// Companion to t_indirectcall, which pins the INDIRECT-edge roots. This one pins
// the other correctness root: a function that is part of the module's public
// surface and is deliberately NOT called from anywhere inside the module.
//
// Neither exported_add nor exported_mul has a single call edge. Walking the call
// graph from main alone marks both dead — which is the right answer for an
// executable and the WRONG answer for a --shared / --staticlib build, where the
// exports are the only roots there are. Dropping them would produce a library
// whose advertised entry points resolve to nothing.
//
// `-dfe-report` on this program must report the export roots as a non-zero count.
// The exit code only proves the program still builds and runs; the number is the
// part that proves the root category is wired.

// exported_via_helper additionally pins TRANSITIVE reachability from an export
// root. The first version of this oracle made every exported function a leaf, so
// it proved only that roots survive -- never that the walk continues THROUGH one.
// A pass that seeded export roots but failed to follow their call edges would have
// passed it while shipping a DLL whose advertised entry point jumps into a hole.
//
// deep_helper is deliberately too large to inline. That matters: at -O1 the
// inliner deletes call edges, so a small callee legitimately disappears from the
// graph and its pruning is correct. A small helper here would have tested the
// inliner, not the root set -- and reading the prune list without accounting for
// that is exactly how this oracle's own author briefly "found" a bug that was not
// there.

#[export]
fn exported_add(a: i64, b: i64) -> i64:
    return a + b

#[export]
fn exported_mul(a: i64, b: i64) -> i64:
    return a * b

fn deep_helper(x: i64) -> i64:
    mut acc = 0 as i64
    mut i = 0 as i64
    while i < 3 as i64:
        acc = acc + x
        if acc > 1000 as i64:
            acc = acc - 1 as i64
        if acc < 0 as i64:
            acc = acc + 2 as i64
        i = i + 1
    return acc

#[export]
fn exported_via_helper(x: i64) -> i64:
    return deep_helper(x)

fn main() -> i64:
    return 42
